#!/bin/sh
# gondo-pi clipboard (VM): copy stdin to your HOST clipboard via OSC 52 (your terminal + zellij
# pass it on). Installed as pbcopy, wl-copy, xclip, xsel and clip in the VM.
# Paste is not supported (terminals don't answer OSC 52 reads): pbpaste/wl-paste print nothing.
case "$(basename "$0")" in
  pbpaste|wl-paste) exit 0 ;;
esac
# xclip -o / xsel -o = paste: nothing to give
for a in "$@"; do case "$a" in -o|--output|-out) exit 0 ;; esac; done
data=$(base64 | tr -d '\n')
# OSC 52 to the controlling terminal (not stdout: may be a pipe)
if { : > /dev/tty; } 2>/dev/null; then
  printf '\033]52;c;%s\a' "$data" > /dev/tty
else
  printf '\033]52;c;%s\a' "$data" >&2      # no controlling tty (e.g. run by pi's bash tool)
fi
